  "result": "The cause was in `findIssueById` in `src/server/repositories/issue-repository.ts`. It accepted `orgId` but its query was `where(eq(issues.id, issueId))`, so any issue id from any organization was returned. The service layer (`getIssue`, `updateIssue`, `assignIssue`, and the rest) relies on that lookup for its tenant boundary, and the `assertOrgScope` check runs only after the row is already loaded.\n\nI changed the query to `and(orgPredicate(issues.orgId, orgId), eq(issues.id, issueId))`, which matches the scoping used by the other lookups in that file. A cross-org id now returns `null`, which `requireFound` turns into a `NotFoundError`, so the user sees the same response as for an id that does not exist.",
